WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.487
An organization hierarchy is a classic recursive example.

00:00:04.487 --> 00:00:09.132
We start with the root employee whose manager ID is NULL.

00:00:09.132 --> 00:00:12.547
Then we find employees who report to that root.

00:00:12.547 --> 00:00:15.777
Then employees who report to those employees.

00:00:15.777 --> 00:00:22.092
Depth tells us the level, and a path string lets us see the route from the top of the hierarchy.

00:00:22.092 --> 00:00:29.167
Recursive CTEs are useful when rows refer to other rows in a hierarchy or graph-like chain.

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:35.297
The anchor establishes the starting set; the recursive term finds the next level.

00:00:35.297 --> 00:00:38.682
Always think about termination and cycles.

00:00:38.682 --> 00:00:43.749
Production hierarchies often need safeguards against malformed relationships.
